From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+openwrt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net airoha xPON upstream PPE flow offload

Upstream flows leaving through the xPON client's net_device (pon0) were
refused: pon0 is not a GDM device, so the flowtable left them on the CPU.
The client now gets an ops.ppe_upstream callback that says where its xmit
would send the flow - VID and P-bit on the fibre, GEM port, T-CONT,
queue - and the FOE entry is written as hw_nat does for FOE_MAGIC_GPON
(ra_nat_entry.c:5136-5145, 5991): the QDMA hardware forward port 2 with
the PSE QoS bit, the T-CONT as channel and NBQ (gpon_wan.c:453-456), the
queue as qid, the GEM port in the etype field and the whole outer TCI in
vlan1 (ra_nat_entry.c:1709, 2893).  The PPPoE header still comes from IB1.

The P-bit handed to the client is the one the CPU path writes: ip_forward()
sets skb->priority from the TOS (net.ipv4.ip_forward_update_priority) and
the VLAN device on pon0 maps it through its egress_qos_map.  The flowtable
carries the DSCP in the tuple, so a DSCP change is a new flow.  A priority
the flowtable carries (FLOW_ACTION_PRIORITY, 708) wins over the DSCP;
without one the DSCP is used for IPv6 as well, whose forwarding leaves
skb->priority 0, so its traffic class still sets the P-bit.

airoha_xpon_ppe_flush() unbinds these flows when the client's
classification changes (rules, VID map, GEMs, T-CONTs) and on unregister;
as for a WED detach the software entries stay, marked stale, and the
flowtable's next REPLACE of a flow that still has traffic rebuilds it.
Bridged flows and double tags stay on the CPU.  Unverified on hardware:
how the etype reaches the GEM field of the QDMA descriptor
(SUPPORT_STAG_FROM_INFO).

Signed-off-by: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+openwrt@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -4116,6 +4116,7 @@ static struct {
 	void *rx_priv;
 	struct net_device *tx_dev;
 	bool ppe_downstream;
+	int (*ppe_upstream)(void *priv, struct airoha_xpon_ppe_us *us);
 } airoha_xpon_client;
 
 static struct airoha_gdm_dev *airoha_xpon_gdm_dev(struct airoha_qdma *qdma)
@@ -4348,6 +4349,7 @@ int airoha_xpon_register(struct net_devi
 		airoha_xpon_client.rx_priv = ops->priv;
 		airoha_xpon_client.tx_dev = ops->tx_dev;
 		airoha_xpon_client.ppe_downstream = ops->ppe_downstream;
+		airoha_xpon_client.ppe_upstream = ops->ppe_upstream;
 	}
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&airoha_xpon_lock, flags);
 
